#HELPS

0 ESHIFT EARTHSHIFT EARTHCONTROL~
Syntax: earthshift <target>
ESHIFT is the same command. Requires Vampire Protean 6 and existing
earthmeld. Travels underground to an eligible standing target elsewhere.
Both rooms must allow travel; combat/timers, restraints, roots,
curses/webs and incompatible planes block it. Players must permit
summoning. Safe/private/solitary destinations and your own familiar
are not shortcuts around the native travel restrictions.
~

0 DISINTEGRATE VAMPIREDISINTEGRATION~
Syntax: disintegrate <target>
Requires Vampire Vicissitude 7. Uses the current opponent when the
native combat variant applies, otherwise the named target here.
Costs one-thirtieth of the caster's blood-pool capacity.
Sets the native disintegration state on an eligible target; this is
not an unconditional administrative SLAY command.
~

0 BEASTFORM VAMPIREBEASTFORM~
Syntax: beastform
Requires Vampire Protean 7. Toggles the native advanced beast form,
including its claw, sight, disguise and flight state.
This is distinct from CHANGE BAT/WOLF/MIST and does not change your
account class or grant the Werewolf parent's complete kit.
~

0 SHADOWFORGE SHADOWWEAPON~
Syntax: shadowforge <slash|pierce|blunt>
Requires Vampire Obtenebration 6 and the native shadow-weapon template.
Creates the corresponding weapon through the game's item system.
It is not permission to copy arbitrary artifacts or other players'
custom equipment. Other combat enchantments keep their own rules.
~

0 FLESHBOND ANIMALFUSION~
Syntax: fleshbond <animal>
        fleshbond
Requires Vampire Animalism 7. Bonds an eligible native animal to the
caster and records its contribution to current and maximum health.
Using the command while bonded attempts to separate it again.
Removal is refused if losing those contributions would be fatal.
Players are not valid bond creatures; not every NPC prototype qualifies.
~

0 LEECH VAMPIRELEECH~
Syntax: leech <target>
Requires Vampire Quietus 6 in the actual handler.
Attempts the native blood-leeching attack on an eligible target here.
Blood, target wards and combat checks apply; it is not free blood
creation or a permanent increase to blood-pool capacity.
~

0 FIST FISTOFCAINE~
Syntax: fist <target>
Requires Vampire Potence 7. Performs the native Fist of Caine unarmed
attack with its action delay and existing combat protections.
It does not train weapon skills or permanently raise base strength.
~

0 EYESOFTHESERPENT SERPENTEYES~
Syntax: eyesoftheserpent <target>
Requires Vampire Serpentis 1. Attempts the native Serpent's Eyes
control/disruption against an eligible target in the room.
The full command is EYESOFTHESERPENT; resistance and protective effects
still apply. It does not grant account or staff permissions.
~

0 MARK MARKOFTHESERPENT~
Syntax: mark <target>
Requires Vampire Serpentis 7. Applies the native Mark of the Serpent
attack/effect to an eligible nearby target.
This is a discipline ability, not the builder's or quest item's
ownership-marking interface.
~

0 ENRAGE VAMPIREPROVOKE~
Syntax: enrage <target>
Requires Vampire Presence 6. Attempts to provoke the target's native
rage response. Existing class, resistance and combat checks apply;
it does not select a new permanent class for the victim.
~

0 TENEBROUS SHADOWFORM~
Syntax: tenebrous
Requires Vampire Obtenebration 7. Toggles the native tenebrous shadow
form and its appearance state. Conflicting polymorphs are rejected.
This is separate from ordinary VANISH concealment and UMBRA travel.
~

0 HORRID ADVANCEDILLUSIONATTACK~
Syntax: horrid <target>
Requires Vampire Chimerstry 7 and an eligible nearby target.
Invokes the native advanced illusion attack with its normal checks.
This command is distinct from the separately restored HORRIDREALITY
ability; matching names do not bypass either power's prerequisites.
~

0 TORMENT VAMPIRESPIRITATTACK~
Syntax: torment <target>
Requires Vampire Necromancy 7. Invokes the native spiritual attack,
including spirit-form interaction and substantial health damage.
It is an attack, not a safe way to remove a friend's spirit form.
Existing target and native combat restrictions remain in force.
~

